# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large run artefacts. All regenerable. saved_models alone reached 641 GB and
# .flash currently holds 41 GB; the disk filled on 2026-09-06 and silently
# broke four training arms. See the disk hygiene section of
# docs/QUEUE_STATUS.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
saved_models/
checkpoints/
wandb/
.flash/
cache/
logs/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# analysis/ and scripts/ used to be ignored wholesale, which hid the table
# generators, the figure scripts and the disk guard that the paper depends on.
# The code is now tracked and only the DATA these scripts emit is ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
analysis/arms/
analysis/baseline_errors/
analysis/**/*.npz
analysis/**/*.npy
analysis/**/*.png
analysis/**/*.pdf

# Generated tables and figures under paper/ ARE tracked. They are small, the
# paper needs them, and they are reproducible with
#   python analysis/make_tables.py
#   python analysis/fig_whitened_3d.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch, backups, stray outputs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
motivation/
*.csv
*.bak
*.pre_*
*.orig
uf.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python, editors, OS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Personal instructions file, not part of the codebase.
CLAUDE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded experiment definitions and launchers. Months of exploratory
# sweeps, almost all abandoned; keeping them adds 180 files of noise to every
# diff. The exceptions are the two files current work depends on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
configs/*
!configs/class_weight.yaml

run_files/*
!run_files/_template.sh

# One-off analysis scripts from directions that were closed. The four kept are
# live tooling: the disk guard and pruner (see the disk hygiene section of
# docs/QUEUE_STATUS.md), the MSP-Podcast build, and the asset prefetcher.
scripts/*
!scripts/disk_guard.sh
!scripts/prune_models.py
!scripts/build_mspp_dataset.py
!scripts/prefetch_assets.py

# Figures are committed as PDF for LaTeX. The PNG copies exist only for
# on-screen viewing and are four times the size.
paper/figures/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes. Handoff prompts, live worklists and design docs for closed
# directions: useful on disk, not worth version history.
#
# RESULTS_LOG.md is the exception. Its 24 sections record measurements that
# cannot be recovered by rerunning anything, for instance that roughly 29
# percent of within-class VAD spread is annotator noise, and that resuming a
# swa_last_n run silently falls back to best_val selection.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/*
!docs/RESULTS_LOG.md
